  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Accenture Federal Services recorded $2.3B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date across 349 awards, with an average award size of $6.6M. Accenture Federal Services obligations are down 28.9% year over year. Accenture Federal Services obligations peaked at $3.4B in FY24 and then moved to $3.2B in FY25 before the current-year total of $2.3B. Accenture Federal Services delivered most obligations in Computer Systems Design Services, which accounts for $2B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Accenture Federal Services also has material obligations in Custom Computer Programming Services at $92.6M and Other Computer Related Services at $90.9M. Accenture Federal Services work in FY2026 to date spans multiple agencies, led by the Department of Defense at $453M and followed by the Department of Education at $338M, the Department of Energy at $317M, and other civilian and cabinet-level buyers.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal buyers of Accenture Federal Services?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of Accenture Federal Services with $453M in obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Education follows with $338M, the Department of Energy with $317M, and the Department of Health and Human Services with $234M. The Department of Veterans Affairs, GSA, DHS, State, Commerce, and Treasury round out the top ten buyers."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services generate the most obligations for Accenture Federal Services?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the dominant market for Accenture Federal Services with $2B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services and Other Computer Related Services account for $92.6M and $90.9M respectively, with additional obligations across consulting, infrastructure, software publishing, engineering, and events."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Accenture Federal Services make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Accenture Federal Services has $2.3B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Accenture Federal Services recorded 349 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $6.6M, and obligations are down 28.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Accenture Federal Services?",
      "a": "Accenture Federal Services sells to a broad set of agencies led by the Department of Defense, which obligated $453M in FY2026 to date. Accenture Federal Services also has significant obligations with the Department of Education at $338M, the Department of Energy at $317M, the Department of Health and Human Services at $234M, and other cabinet-level and civilian agencies."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Accenture Federal Services sell to the government?",
      "a": "Accenture Federal Services primarily sells Computer Systems Design Services, which generated $2B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Accenture Federal Services also sells Custom Computer Programming Services at $92.6M, Other Computer Related Services at $90.9M, consulting and management services, computing infrastructure and hosting, software publishing, engineering services, and event organization."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which Accenture Federal Services contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Accenture Federal Services has multiple contracts across markets and agencies; the facts list largest-award and expiring-contract tables as total contract values rather than current obligations. Accenture Federal Services obligations by fiscal year show $3.4B in FY24 and $3.2B in FY25 before the current FY26 total of $2.3B, which may indicate timing and lifecycle effects on contract expirations."
    }
